{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l) # Create a sorted copy of the input list.\n    n = len(sorted_l)    # Determine the number of elements in the list.\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # For an odd number of elements, the median is the middle element.\n        return sorted_l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        # For an even number of elements, the median is the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        avg = (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0 # Perform float division to calculate the average.\n\n        # Return the average as an integer if it's a whole number, otherwise return as a float.\n        if avg.is_integer():\n            return int(avg)\n        else:\n            return avg\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def _sort_list(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts the input list in ascending order.\"\"\"\n    return sorted(l)\n\ndef _calculate_odd_median(sorted_list: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Finds the middle element of a sorted list with an odd number of elements.\"\"\"\n    n = len(sorted_list)\n    return float(sorted_list[n // 2])\n\ndef _calculate_even_median(sorted_list: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the average of the two middle elements of a sorted list with an even number of elements.\n    For an even list of length N, it averages elements at 0-indexed positions N/2 and N/2 + 1.\"\"\"\n    n = len(sorted_list)\n    # The example `median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])` yielding `15.0` implies these indices.\n    mid1 = sorted_list[n // 2 -1]\n    mid2 = sorted_list[n // 2]\n    return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n\ndef _format_output(value: float):\n    \"\"\"Converts a float value to an integer if it represents a whole number, otherwise retaining it as a float.\"\"\"\n    if value == int(value):\n        return int(value)\n    return value\n\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_list = _sort_list(l)\n    n = len(sorted_list)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        raw_median_value = _calculate_odd_median(sorted_list)\n    else:\n        raw_median_value = _calculate_even_median(sorted_list)\n\n    return _format_output(raw_median_value)"}
