{"task_id": "HumanEval/87", "solution": "```python\ndef get_row(lst: list[list[int]], x: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds occurrences of an integer x in a nested list and returns their 0-indexed coordinates.\n    The list is sorted primarily by row ascending, secondarily by column descending.\n    \"\"\"\n    found_coordinates = []\n    for row_idx, row in enumerate(lst):\n        for col_idx, element in enumerate(row):\n            if element == x:\n                found_coordinates.append((row_idx, col_idx))\n\n    # Sort primarily by row ascending (coord[0]), and secondarily by column descending (-coord[1]).\n    found_coordinates.sort(key=lambda coord: (coord[0], -coord[1]))\n\n    return found_coordinates\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "```python\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Processes an input string by sorting characters within each word in ascending ASCII order.\n    Preserves word order and blank space positioning.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_parts = []\n    current_word_chars = []\n    in_word_state = False\n\n    for char in s:\n        if char == ' ':\n            # If a word just ended, process it\n            if in_word_state:\n                current_word_chars.sort()\n                result_parts.append(\"\".join(current_word_chars))\n                current_word_chars = []\n                in_word_state = False\n            # Append the space to preserve its position\n            result_parts.append(char)\n        else:\n            # If a new word is starting, set the state\n            if not in_word_state:\n                in_word_state = True\n            # Add character to the current word\n            current_word_chars.append(char)\n\n    # After the loop, handle any pending word at the end of the string\n    if in_word_state:\n        current_word_chars.sort()\n        result_parts.append(\"\".join(current_word_chars))\n\n    # Join all processed parts to form the final string\n    return \"\".join(result_parts)\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts an array of non-negative integers based on the parity of the sum of its first and last elements.\n    Returns a new sorted array, leaving the original unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n    if n == 1:\n        return list(array) # Return a copy of the single-element array\n\n    first_element = array[0]\n    last_element = array[-1]\n    sum_val = first_element + last_element\n\n    if sum_val % 2 != 0:  # Sum is odd, sort in ascending order\n        return sorted(array)\n    else:  # Sum is even, sort in descending order\n        return sorted(array, reverse=True)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/87", "solution": "def get_row(lst, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds occurrences of x in a nested list and returns their 0-indexed (row, column) coordinates.\n    Coordinates are sorted primarily by row ascending, then by column descending.\n    \"\"\"\n    found_coordinates = []\n\n    for row_index, row in enumerate(lst):\n        for col_index, element in enumerate(row):\n            if element == x:\n                found_coordinates.append((row_index, col_index))\n\n    # Sort coordinates: primary by row ascending, secondary by column descending.\n    # Sorting by -column_index achieves descending order for columns.\n    found_coordinates.sort(key=lambda coord: (coord[0], -coord[1]))\n\n    return found_coordinates"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of non-negative integers, return a copy of the given array after sorting,\n    you will sort the given array in ascending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is odd,\n    or sort it in descending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is even.\n\n    Note:\n    * don't change the given array.\n\n    Examples:\n    * sort_array([]) => []\n    * sort_array([5]) => [5]\n    * sort_array([2, 4, 3, 0, 1, 5]) => [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n    * sort_array([2, 4, 3, 0, 1, 5, 6]) => [6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0]\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return []\n\n    if len(array) == 1:\n        return array[:]\n\n    copied_arr = array[:]\n    sum_first_last = array[0] + array[-1]\n\n    if sum_first_last % 2 == 1: # Odd sum, sort ascending\n        copied_arr.sort(reverse=False)\n    else: # Even sum, sort descending\n        copied_arr.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    return copied_arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "```python\ndef _shift_char(char: str, shift: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Shifts a lowercase English alphabet character by a given amount, with wrap-around.\"\"\"\n    start_char_code = ord('a')\n    char_index = ord(char) - start_char_code\n    new_char_index = (char_index + shift) % 26\n    return chr(new_char_index + start_char_code)\n\ndef encrypt(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Encrypts a string by shifting lowercase English alphabet characters down by four positions.\"\"\"\n    encrypted_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            encrypted_chars.append(_shift_char(char, 4))\n        else:\n            encrypted_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(encrypted_chars)\n```"}
