{"task_id": "HumanEval/93", "solution": "```python\ndef encode(message):\n    \"\"\"\n    This function encodes a message by swapping the case of alphabetic characters\n    and replacing vowels with a letter two places ahead, then swapping its case.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Internal constants for efficient lookups\n    _VOWELS = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u', 'A', 'E', 'I', 'O', 'U'}\n    _ALPHABET_LIST = [chr(i) for i in range(ord('a'), ord('z') + 1)]  # Lowercase English alphabet\n    _ALPHABET_MAP = {char: i for i, char in enumerate(_ALPHABET_LIST)}\n\n    def _swap_case(char_val: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Swaps the case of an alphabetic character.\"\"\"\n        return char_val.swapcase()\n\n    def _is_vowel(char_val: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a character is an English vowel (case-insensitive).\"\"\"\n        return char_val.isalpha() and char_val in _VOWELS\n\n    def _get_letter_ahead(char_val: str, places: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns the letter 'places' ahead of char_val in the alphabet,\n        preserving the original case.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not char_val.isalpha():\n            return char_val\n\n        is_upper = char_val.isupper()\n        char_lower = char_val.lower()\n\n        original_index = _ALPHABET_MAP.get(char_lower)\n        # This check guards against non-alphabetic characters not caught by .isalpha(),\n        # or characters outside 'a'-'z' range if input constraints were looser.\n        if original_index is None:\n            return char_val\n\n        new_index = (original_index + places) % 26\n        replacement_char_lower = _ALPHABET_LIST[new_index]\n\n        return replacement_char_lower.upper() if is_upper else replacement_char_lower\n\n    result_chars = []\n    for char in message:\n        processed_char = ''\n        if _is_vowel(char):\n            # For vowels, first get the shifted character preserving original case,\n            # then apply the global case swap to the shifted character.\n            temp_char = _get_letter_ahead(char, 2)\n            processed_char = _swap_case(temp_char)\n        elif char.isalpha():\n            # For non-vowel alphabetic characters, just swap their case.\n            processed_char = _swap_case(char)\n        else:\n            # For non-alphabetic characters (e.g., spaces, numbers), preserve them.\n            processed_char = char\n        result_chars.append(processed_char)\n\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```\n"}
