{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "```python\ndef is_bored(S):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts boredoms in a string, where a boredom is a sentence starting with \"I\".\n    Sentences are delimited by '.', '?' or '!'.\n    \"\"\"\n    boredoms = 0\n    current_sentence_chars = []\n    delimiters = {'.', '?', '!'}\n\n    for char in S:\n        if char in delimiters:\n            sentence = \"\".join(current_sentence_chars).strip()\n            if sentence:\n                # Check if the first word of the sentence is \"I\"\n                words = sentence.split(maxsplit=1)\n                if words and words[0] == \"I\":\n                    boredoms += 1\n            current_sentence_chars = [] # Reset for next sentence\n        else:\n            current_sentence_chars.append(char)\n\n    # Handle the last sentence if the string does not end with a delimiter\n    if current_sentence_chars:\n        sentence = \"\".join(current_sentence_chars).strip()\n        if sentence:\n            words = sentence.split(maxsplit=1)\n            if words and words[0] == \"I\":\n                boredoms += 1\n\n    return boredoms\n```\n"}
