{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the closest integer to a given number string,\n    rounding away from zero for equidistant values.\n    \"\"\"\n    float_value = float(value)\n    floor_int = math.floor(float_value)\n    ceil_int = math.ceil(float_value)\n\n    # Check for equidistant case (X.5)\n    if abs(float_value - floor_int) == 0.5:\n        if float_value > 0: # Positive X.5, round up (away from zero)\n            return ceil_int\n        else: # Negative X.5, round down (away from zero)\n            return floor_int\n    else:\n        # Standard rounding to nearest integer\n        if abs(float_value - floor_int) < abs(float_value - ceil_int):\n            return floor_int\n        else:\n            return ceil_int\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the closest integer to the input string `value`. If equidistant, it rounds away from zero\n    (e.g., 14.5 to 15, -14.5 to -15).\n    \"\"\"\n    parsed_number = float(value)\n\n    integer_part = int(parsed_number)\n    fractional_part = abs(parsed_number - integer_part)\n\n    if fractional_part == 0.5:\n        # Round away from zero for .5 cases\n        if parsed_number > 0:\n            return int(parsed_number + 0.5)\n        else:  # parsed_number <= 0\n            return int(parsed_number - 0.5)\n    else:\n        # For all other fractional parts, use standard rounding.\n        return round(parsed_number)\n```"}
