{"task_id": "HumanEval/100", "solution": "```python\ndef make_a_pile(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, make a pile of n levels of stones.\n    The number of stones in subsequent levels increases by 2, maintaining n's initial parity.\n    \"\"\"\n    stone_counts_list = []\n    current_stones = n\n    stone_counts_list.append(current_stones)\n\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        current_stones += 2\n        stone_counts_list.append(current_stones)\n\n    return stone_counts_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/100", "solution": "```python\ndef make_a_pile(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer `n`, this function makes a pile of `n` levels of stones.\n    The first level has `n` stones, and subsequent levels follow the next odd/even number rule.\n    \"\"\"\n    pile_levels = [n]\n\n    # The rule for subsequent levels simplifies to always adding 2,\n    # as adding 2 maintains the parity of the previous number,\n    # thereby satisfying the 'next odd' or 'next even' requirement based on n's initial parity.\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        current_stones = pile_levels[-1]\n        next_stones = current_stones + 2\n        pile_levels.append(next_stones)\n\n    return pile_levels\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/94", "solution": "def is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime.\n    Returns True for prime numbers, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n <= 3: # 2 and 3 are prime\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:\n        return False\n    i = 5\n    # Loop up to sqrt(n) for efficiency\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 6\n    return True\n\ndef sum_digits(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the digits of a number.\n    Sums each individual digit of the given integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = 0\n    # For primes, n will always be a positive integer here.\n    while n > 0:\n        total += n % 10\n        n //= 10\n    return total\n\ndef skjkasdkd(lst):\n    \"\"\"Finds the largest prime in a list and returns the sum of its digits.\n    Returns 0 if no prime numbers are found in the list.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest_prime = -1 # Initialize with a value that no prime can be (primes are > 1)\n\n    for num in lst:\n        if is_prime(num):\n            if num > largest_prime:\n                largest_prime = num\n\n    if largest_prime == -1: # No prime number was found in the list\n        return 0\n    else:\n        return sum_digits(largest_prime)"}
