{"task_id": "HumanEval/103", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Union\n\ndef rounded_avg(n: int, m: int) -> Union[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"You are given two positive integers n and m, and your task is to compute the\n    average of the integers from n through m (including n and m).\n    Round the answer to the nearest integer and convert that to binary.\n    If n is greater than m, return -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Return -1 if the starting integer n is greater than the ending integer m.\n    if n > m:\n        return -1\n\n    # Calculate the sum of integers from n to m and their count.\n    count = m - n + 1\n    sum_of_range = (n + m) * count / 2\n\n    # Compute the average, round it to the nearest integer, and convert to binary.\n    average = sum_of_range / count\n    rounded_integer = round(average)\n    return bin(rounded_integer)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/102", "solution": "```python\ndef choose_num(x, y):\n    \"\"\"This function finds the biggest even integer within the inclusive range [x, y].\n    It returns -1 if no such number exists or if the input range is invalid.\"\"\"\n\n    # Validate inputs: x and y must be positive, and x must not be greater than y.\n    if x <= 0 or y <= 0 or x > y:\n        return -1\n\n    # Iterate downwards from y to x to find the largest even number efficiently.\n    for num in range(y, x - 1, -1):\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return num  # Return the first (largest) even number found.\n\n    # If the loop completes, no even number was found in the range.\n    return -1\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/102", "solution": "```python\ndef choose_num(x: int, y: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the biggest even integer in the inclusive range [x, y].\n    Returns -1 if no even number exists within the range.\n    \"\"\"\n    start = min(x, y)\n    end = max(x, y)\n\n    result = -1\n    for i in range(end, start - 1, -1):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            result = i\n            break\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/96", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef is_prime(number):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime.\n    Efficiently checks divisibility up to the square root of the number.\"\"\"\n    if number < 2:\n        return False\n    # Check for divisibility from 2 up to the square root of the number\n    for i in range(2, int(math.sqrt(number)) + 1):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef count_up_to(n):\n    \"\"\"Implement a function that takes a non-negative integer and returns an array of the first n\n    integers that are prime numbers and less than n.\n    for example:\n    count_up_to(5) => [2,3]\n    count_up_to(11) => [2,3,5,7]\n    count_up_to(0) => []\n    count_up_to(20) => [2,3,5,7,11,13,17,19]\n    count_up_to(1) => []\n    count_up_to(18) => [2,3,5,7,11,13,17]\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return []\n\n    prime_numbers = []\n    # Iterate from 2 up to n-1\n    for number in range(2, n):\n        if is_prime(number):\n            prime_numbers.append(number)\n    return prime_numbers\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/103", "solution": "```python\ndef rounded_avg(n, m):\n    \"\"\"Computes the average of integers from n to m, rounds it, and converts to binary.\n    Returns -1 if n is greater than m.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n > m:\n        return -1\n\n    count = m - n + 1\n    total_sum = (n + m) * count / 2.0\n\n    raw_average = total_sum / count\n\n    # Round the average to the nearest integer using the \"round half up\" rule.\n    rounded_average = int(raw_average + 0.5)\n\n    return bin(rounded_average)\n```"}
