{"task_id": "HumanEval/137", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Union\n\n# Helper class for parsing various real number representations to a float.\nclass _RealNumberParser:\n    def parse_to_float(self, value: Union[int, float, str]) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Converts an int, float, or string (with '.' or ',' decimal) to a float.\"\"\"\n        if isinstance(value, str):\n            # Handle both '.' and ',' as decimal separators for strings.\n            cleaned_value = value.replace(',', '.')\n            return float(cleaned_value)\n        # Directly convert int or float to float.\n        return float(value)\n\n# Helper class to encapsulate an original value and its comparable float representation.\nclass _InputWrapper:\n    # Use a single parser instance for efficiency across wrappers.\n    _parser = _RealNumberParser()\n\n    def __init__(self, value: Union[int, float, str]):\n        \"\"\"Initializes with the original value and its float representation for comparison.\"\"\"\n        self.original_value = value\n        self.comparable_float = self._parser.parse_to_float(value)\n\ndef compare_one(a: Union[int, float, str], b: Union[int, float, str]) -> Union[int, float, str, None]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compares two real numbers (int, float, or string) and returns the numerically larger value\n    preserving its original type, or None if they are equal.\n    \"\"\"\n    wrapper_a = _InputWrapper(a)\n    wrapper_b = _InputWrapper(b)\n\n    if wrapper_a.comparable_float > wrapper_b.comparable_float:\n        return wrapper_a.original_value\n    elif wrapper_b.comparable_float > wrapper_a.comparable_float:\n        return wrapper_b.original_value\n    else: # wrapper_a.comparable_float == wrapper_b.comparable_float\n        return None\n```"}
