{"task_id": "HumanEval/144", "solution": "```python\ndef simplify(x, n):\n    \"\"\"Checks if the product of two fractions, x and n, is a whole number.\n    Returns True if the product is a whole number, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n\n    # 1. Parse x\n    x_numerator_str, x_denominator_str = x.split('/')\n    x_num = int(x_numerator_str)\n    x_den = int(x_denominator_str)\n\n    # 2. Parse n\n    n_numerator_str, n_denominator_str = n.split('/')\n    n_num = int(n_numerator_str)\n    n_den = int(n_denominator_str)\n\n    # 3. Calculate Product Components\n    product_num = x_num * n_num\n    product_den = x_den * n_den\n\n    # 4. Check for Whole Number Result and 5. Return Result\n    return product_num % product_den == 0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/142", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_squares(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    This function processes a list of integers, applying transformations based on index and returning their sum.\n    It squares elements at indices multiple of 3, cubes elements at indices multiple of 4 (but not 3), and leaves others unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for index, value in enumerate(lst):\n        modified_value = value\n        if index % 3 == 0:\n            modified_value = value * value\n        elif index % 4 == 0:  # This condition implies index % 3 != 0 due to the 'elif'\n            modified_value = value * value * value\n        # else: modified_value remains unchanged (original value)\n\n        total_sum += modified_value\n    return total_sum\n```"}
