{"task_id": "HumanEval/153", "solution": "```python\nclass Extension:\n    \"\"\"Represents an extension with its name and calculated strength.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, name: str, strength: int):\n        self.name = name\n        self.strength = strength\n\ndef _calculate_extension_strength(extension_name: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the strength of an extension based on CAP - SM.\"\"\"\n    cap_count = 0\n    sm_count = 0\n    for char in extension_name:\n        if 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            cap_count += 1\n        elif 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            sm_count += 1\n    return cap_count - sm_count\n\ndef Strongest_Extension(class_name: str, extensions: list[str]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Finds the strongest extension and returns it with the class name.\"\"\"\n\n    max_strength = -float('inf')\n    strongest_extension_name = \"\"\n\n    for extension_name in extensions:\n        # Create an Extension object as specified in the design.\n        strength_value = _calculate_extension_strength(extension_name)\n        current_extension_obj = Extension(extension_name, strength_value)\n\n        # Determine the strongest extension, prioritizing the first one for ties.\n        if current_extension_obj.strength > max_strength:\n            max_strength = current_extension_obj.strength\n            strongest_extension_name = current_extension_obj.name\n\n    return f\"{class_name}.{strongest_extension_name}\"\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "```python\ndef double_the_difference(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sums the squares of numbers in the list that are non-negative and either odd or zero.\n    Filters out non-integer numbers, negative numbers, and even non-zero numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return 0\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for item in lst:\n        # Filter non-integer numbers (e.g., 3.5, assuming item is a number)\n        if item != int(item):\n            continue\n\n        # Filter negative numbers\n        if item < 0:\n            continue\n\n        # Filter even and non-zero numbers (keep if odd or zero)\n        if item % 2 == 0 and item != 0:\n            continue\n\n        # Calculate square and add to total\n        total_sum += item ** 2\n\n    return total_sum\n```"}
